  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "The spin only magnetic moment of the complex present in Fehling&#39;s reagent is____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.</mo></math> (Round off your answer to the nearest integer)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Fehling&#39;s solution consists of two parts A and B. &nbsp;Fehling&rsquo;s solution A&nbsp; is deep blue colour&nbsp;due to the bis(tartrate) complex of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>.&nbsp;Fehling&#39;s solution B is the Rochelle salt (potassium sodium tartrate tetrahydrate) serves as a chelating agent in the solution.</p><p>Fehling solution is a complex of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>9</mn></msup></math></p><p>Number&nbsp;of unpaired&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Magnetic</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Moment</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>73</mn><mi>BM</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
